    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-5",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q5",
        "itemBody": "<p>When analyzing investment returns, which of the following statements is correct?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "72e7bc78-31e0-4ee2-9c3b-468ed038e174",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The geometric mean will exceed the arithmetic mean for a series with non-zero variance.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "868626a9-aac8-4098-9aa3-ca3bcaebb447",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The geometric mean measures an investment’s compound rate of growth over multiple periods.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "6d8483b1-e9a2-4aef-a47e-18b37a90cf03",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The arithmetic mean measures an investment’s terminal value over multiple periods.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "72e7bc78-31e0-4ee2-9c3b-468ed038e174"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-6",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q6",
        "itemBody": "<p>A fund had the following returns over the past 10 years: Year Return 1 4.5% 2 6.0% 3 1.5% 4 −2.0% 5 0.0% 6 4.5% 7 3.5% 8 2.5% 9 5.5% 10 4.0% The difference between the arithmetic and geometric mean returns over the 10 years is closest to which of the following?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "3025b5f5-2d2d-4ebd-a4da-7388b1059814",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The arithmetic return is 3 bps higher.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "52cd3911-b00e-49c2-9c8f-ab2bc01eba64",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The returns are the same (i.e., 0 bps difference).</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "8aa92213-fe67-4c5e-ae8e-82eff841af35",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The geometric return is 3 bps higher.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "3025b5f5-2d2d-4ebd-a4da-7388b1059814"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-7",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q7",
        "itemBody": "<p>The price of a stock at t = 0 is CNY208.25, and at t = 1, it is CNY186.75. The continuously compounded rate of return, r1,T for the stock is closest to:</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "6a694e4f-bca6-4399-ab08-3a382bb6c3bb",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. −10.89%.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "da7329bd-14b9-46dc-9405-172bad3544ac",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. −10.32%.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "41862e4c-07fe-4901-bd3b-88366f2e9102",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. 10.90%.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "6a694e4f-bca6-4399-ab08-3a382bb6c3bb"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-8",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q8",
        "itemBody": "<p>What does the geometric mean return in investment analysis signify?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "87550e74-a11e-4a12-adfb-4d494f8ba44f",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The simple average of all holding period returns.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "d7a94259-ce02-49f2-84c0-f22926a29e37",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The average rate at which an asset’s value grows over time, accounting for the compounding of returns.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "34e225fc-053c-4dca-95f1-d9bceb330863",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The return earned by a manager after the deduction of trading expenses and commissions.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "87550e74-a11e-4a12-adfb-4d494f8ba44f"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-9",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q9",
        "itemBody": "<p>For investment analysis purposes, logarithmic returns:</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "3f0bc7cb-6e3c-4604-8e6d-6dcb9613896d",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. equal the sum of periodic geometric returns over the investment period.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "502ccfb6-5c60-4d1c-9564-75395e34cc38",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. adjust the final value of an investment for inflation over multiple periods.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "391f5985-41e3-47e6-a20e-4648f72c0843",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. require taking the natural logarithm of the ratio of the final value to the initial value.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "3f0bc7cb-6e3c-4604-8e6d-6dcb9613896d"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-10",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q10",
        "itemBody": "<p>A major limitation of annualizing returns for investments is the implicit assumption that:</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "d06d2398-1c96-449f-a6da-d88757bce114",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. periodic returns are constant.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "85eb52ac-fadd-4ec9-a29b-9637f48674e1",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. capital distributions are not reinvested.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "504a447f-d0c5-4f50-ad7f-38c5d8c7af1a",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. arithmetic and geometric returns are identical.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "d06d2398-1c96-449f-a6da-d88757bce114"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-11",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q11",
        "itemBody": "<p>Which statement accurately reflects the distinction between ex ante, or expected returns, and ex post, actual or realized, returns in investment decision-making?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "ab2abfc1-c025-46b9-a5ff-be744e7ec289",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. Expected returns are forecasts made before the returns are realized, while actual returns are the realized returns earned by the end of the investment period.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "34db20cc-3a50-492b-a169-88fb30368077",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. Expected returns influence actual returns directly, ensuring that future investment returns are known.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "db12273d-988e-4e45-85c5-652c6f494741",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. Expected returns, based on historical data and market analysis, predict realized returns with certainty.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "ab2abfc1-c025-46b9-a5ff-be744e7ec289"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-12",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q12",
        "itemBody": "<p>What is the primary difference between gross return and net return in investment analysis?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "ac7e0776-e83e-4432-b5f2-b1f9dfdf8ecd",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. Gross return includes management fees, while net return does not.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "29fe5fdd-7dfb-44f6-9494-1cecf81e1546",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. Net return accounts for management as well as administrative and other miscellaneous fees.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "ac8edda7-e4e8-43bb-be7e-b8a025c2170e",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. Gross return adjusts for inflation, whereas net return does not.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "ac7e0776-e83e-4432-b5f2-b1f9dfdf8ecd"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-13",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q13",
        "itemBody": "<p>Which of the following best describes a risk-free rate in the context of required rate of return?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "20047177-aba9-48bb-99ef-64ac05fd84e2",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. It is the additional return expected for bearing extra risks.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "be9587b5-1101-42b0-ab5c-440649b90853",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. It is the return on an investment without any default or reinvestment risk, typically represented by short- term government bonds.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "417d43ac-76bb-42f6-aa4e-bdcb45860a42",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. It is the minimum return an investor expects to compensate for delayed consumption</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "20047177-aba9-48bb-99ef-64ac05fd84e2"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-14",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q14",
        "itemBody": "<p>What drives the risk premia in investments?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "08ebadd5-25d3-4912-a468-e7d021889d84",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The certainty of investment outcomes</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "629c627a-fa0f-4663-9471-5bbc0ef176cc",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The difference between expected and actual returns</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "bb5b7d36-bbf3-46b2-bbfd-b1281310a7ef",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The consensus financial indicator expectations</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "08ebadd5-25d3-4912-a468-e7d021889d84"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          }
        },
        "scoringAlgorithm": "Equivalence",
        "interactionTypeSlug": "choice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-1-15",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod1-Q15",
        "itemBody": "<p>When evaluating investment returns, which statement is accurate?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "d6f85d96-a462-4446-89b9-f6859ef53cbd",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. The geometric mean is higher than the arithmetic mean when there’s variability in returns.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "868ef168-e772-4814-8525-e03c5c17f75b",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. The geometric mean calculates the compound growth rate of an investment across several periods.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "60c86e17-0a67-4c55-bd97-751857944727",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The arithmetic mean calculates the final value of an investment across multiple periods.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "d6f85d96-a462-4446-89b9-f6859ef53cbd"
        },
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
