        "itemBody": "<p>An investor purchases 100 shares of stock at $40 per share. The investor holds the shares for exactly one year and then sells all of them at $41.50 per share. On the date of sale, the investor receives dividends totaling $200. The holding period return (HPR) on the investment is closest to:</p>",
